# KR-AV Ethics Console

Korea-focused Moral Machine successor: a forced-choice AV dilemma platform
extended with **free-text reasoning + NLP analysis**, so the platform
captures not just *what* people choose but *why*, structured into
ethical value-frames (utilitarian, age-based, legal-status, social
inclusion, etc.).

## Quickstart
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
# -> http://localhost:5000
```

## Structure
```
app.py                   # Flask app: auth, routes, API, background insight worker
scenarios/
  scenario_engine.py      # Korea-specific dilemma generator + preference-weight scoring
nlp/
  insights.py              # Comment sentiment + ethical value-frame tagging + aggregation
templates/                # Jinja2 templates (dark "traffic console" UI)
static/css/style.css      # Design system (see tokens at top of file)
static/js/judge.js        # Client-side dilemma flow
data/                     # SQLite DBs (users.db, responses.db) + insights cache, gitignored in practice
docs/BRAINSTORM.md         # Novel-idea backlog for where to take this next
```

## How it differs from moralmachine.net
- Localized character set + road contexts for Korea (delivery riders,
  hagwon shuttle students, senior-center elderly, migrant workers, etc.)
  — see `scenarios/scenario_engine.py`.
- Every dilemma optionally collects **free-text reasoning**, analyzed by
  `nlp/insights.py` into sentiment + keywords + ethical value-frame tags.
- `/insights` is a public aggregate dashboard of those NLP signals across
  all respondents (anonymized).
- `/results` is the per-user Moral-Machine-style "your preferences" page,
  computed from actual logged judgments.

## NLP pipeline
Ships with a transparent lexicon/rule-based Korean+English sentiment and
value-frame tagger (`USE_TRANSFORMERS = False` in `nlp/insights.py`) so the
app runs with zero heavy dependencies. Swap in a real model by installing
`konlpy` + `transformers` (e.g. `beomi/KcELECTRA-base` for sentiment,
`Okt`/`Mecab` for morphological keyword extraction) and flipping that flag —
the function signature (`analyze_comment(text) -> dict`) doesn't change, so
nothing else in the app needs to be touched.

## Next steps
See `docs/BRAINSTORM.md` for a prioritized backlog of novel directions
(probabilistic harm framing, context-conditioned preference weights,
deliberation/jury mode, cross-cultural comparison mode, etc.).
